ange to match plural instructions.","C":"Adjectives do not normally add a plural -s in English.","D":"Clearly is an adverb, not the adjective before instructions."}}},{"id":"ae66766b-4791-5701-aea0-f16c56a9f698","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose the usual neutral adjective order for the box of supplies used to restore the old portrait.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"a wooden old small box"},{"id":"B","text":"an old wooden small box"},{"id":"C","text":"a small wooden olds box"},{"id":"D","text":"a small old wooden box"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Order these categories: **size, age, material**.","explanation":"The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**.","keywords":["neutral-adjective-order"],"skill":"neutral-adjective-order","contextKey":"adjective-order-2","fingerprint":"6593aef49985ab0967022a5b0c543ac3498e3227520ba432ac9faea0d4327cd9","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Order these categories: **size, age, material**.","The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**.","Choose **a small old wooden box**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"This reverses the usual size–age–material ordering.","B":"Small normally comes before age and material in the neutral sequence.","C":"Old does not take a plural -s and normally precedes the material adjective.","D":"The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**."}}},{"id":"952dcc02-9ae5-5e38-a967-4e90b8b1226a","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose an adjective after be: “The assistant is ____ of restoring the old portrait alone.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"afraid"},{"id":"B","text":"fear"},{"id":"C","text":"fearfully"},{"id":"D","text":"afraids"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The slot after **is** describes a state and is followed by the preposition **of**.","explanation":"**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","keywords":["predicative-adjective"],"skill":"predicative-adjective","contextKey":"adjective-order-2","fingerprint":"7a97c935db1caaa330753c9f4599236bd7545b06208dec9671771201f7a7f9d0","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The slot after **is** describes a state and is followed by the preposition **of**.","**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","Choose **afraid**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","B":"Fear is a noun or verb, not this adjective after is.","C":"Fearfully is an adverb and does not fill the adjective slot.","D":"Afraid does not take an -s ending."}}},{"id":"34d8f11a-bcf7-5b74-a603-cfbb25253c38","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Describe the task’s quality: “The plan to measure the garden fence sounds ____.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"use"},{"id":"B","text":"useful"},{"id":"C","text":"usefully"},{"id":"D","text":"usefulness"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"The sentence evaluates **the plan**, not how someone makes a sound.","explanation":"Sounds is a linking verb here, so **useful** describes the plan.","keywords":["adjective-linking"],"skill":"adjective-linking","contextKey":"adjective-order-3","fingerprint":"012f19858c035800123187664b64214ca617e8b981991ea799b6640f49f16c8d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The sentence evaluates **the plan**, 