 usual neutral adjective order for the box of supplies used to measure the garden fence.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"an old wooden small box"},{"id":"B","text":"a small wooden olds box"},{"id":"C","text":"a small old wooden box"},{"id":"D","text":"a wooden old small box"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Order these categories: **size, age, material**.","explanation":"The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**.","keywords":["neutral-adjective-order"],"skill":"neutral-adjective-order","contextKey":"adjective-order-3","fingerprint":"b83d0bda2e01cfb6461e152a4f281ffde886f4d0952215e0b49b4e7bfe59ffde","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Order these categories: **size, age, material**.","The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**.","Choose **a small old wooden box**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Small normally comes before age and material in the neutral sequence.","B":"Old does not take a plural -s and normally precedes the material adjective.","C":"The ordinary sequence here is **size → age → material → noun**.","D":"This reverses the usual size–age–material ordering."}}},{"id":"1b98cc7a-2355-583d-a510-a264a85e5f32","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose an adjective after be: “The assistant is ____ of measuring the garden fence alone.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"fearfully"},{"id":"B","text":"afraids"},{"id":"C","text":"afraid"},{"id":"D","text":"fear"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The slot after **is** describes a state and is followed by the preposition **of**.","explanation":"**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","keywords":["predicative-adjective"],"skill":"predicative-adjective","contextKey":"adjective-order-3","fingerprint":"4e4173f16f8e80442d1ae018f332102b8b9bb760074995c4accdf49ff92977fb","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The slot after **is** describes a state and is followed by the preposition **of**.","**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","Choose **afraid**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Fearfully is an adverb and does not fill the adjective slot.","B":"Afraid does not take an -s ending.","C":"**Afraid of** is a predicative adjective pattern describing the assistant’s state.","D":"Fear is a noun or verb, not this adjective after is."}}},{"id":"d4cfd21a-57a4-5fbb-aea5-2d789321e77e","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Describe the task’s quality: “The plan to translate the travel leaflet sounds ____.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"usefully"},{"id":"B","text":"usefulness"},{"id":"C","text":"use"},{"id":"D","text":"useful"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The sentence evaluates **the plan**, not how someone makes a sound.","explanation":"Sounds is a linking verb here, so **useful** describes the plan.","keywords":["adjective-linking"],"skill":"adjective-linking","contextKey":"adjective-order-4","fingerprint":"7eabf6065956bab4d76c95fa72cd872f692948be596fe3a8ddd7b6ea5058bc7a","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The sentence evaluates **the plan**, not how someone makes a sound.","Sounds is a linking verb here, so **useful** describes the plan.","Choose **useful**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Usefully is an adverb and would describe manner, not the plan’s quality after linking sounds.","B":"Usefulness is a noun, not the required adjective.","C":"Use is not the descriptive adjective needed here.","D":"Sounds is a linking verb here, so **useful** describes the plan."}}},{"id":"d2b8715a-968e-5bc5-a45d-3031f2abacc6","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Complete the plural noun phrase: “We need ____ instructions to translate the travel leaflet.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"clearly"},{"id":"B","text":"clearness"},{"id":"C","text":"clear"},{"id":"D","text":"clears"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The noun is plural, but the **adjective stays unchanged**.","explanation":"The adjective **clear** does not change to match plural instructions.","keywords":["adjective-number"],"skill":"adjective-number","contextKey":"adjective-order-4","fingerprint":"9e537eb03ee5aeff51b74d77a2f48d487167addef494b9aa42bf7fa4dbcd55b4","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-adjectives"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The noun is plural, but the **adjective stays unchanged**.","The adjective **clear** does not change to match plural instructions.","Choose **clear**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Clearly is an adverb, not the adjective before instructions.","B":"Clearness is a noun and does not supply this adjective.","C":"The adjective **clear** does not change to match plural instructions.","D":"Adjectives do not normally add a plural -s in English."}}},{"id":"25dd1126-a733-5aae-acd5-6523f7267568","topicSlug":"adjective-order","level":"A2","prompt":"Choose the usual neutral adjective order for the box of supplies used to translate the travel leaflet.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"a small wooden olds box"},{"id":"B","text":"a small old wooden box"},{"id":"C","text":"a wooden old small box"},{"id":"D","text":"an old wooden 